    "insights": [
      "Mathlib has Basis.SmithNormalForm and Submodule.smithNormalForm in LinearAlgebra.FreeModule.PID",
      "Parent proof uses custom axioms for SNF existence and solvability. These could potentially be replaced by Mathlib SNF.",
      "Generalization to PIDs: replace ℤ with R [IsPrincipalIdealRing R] and use GCDMonoid/EuclideanDomain API",
      "snf_1x2_invariant_factor: d|gcd(a,b) because a=u*d*V[0,0] and b=u*d*V[0,1] from A=U*D*V decomposition",
      "gcd(a,b)|d because det(V)=±1 implies a*V[1,1]-b*V[1,0]=±u*d, so d is a linear combination of a,b",
      "Main Lean challenge: extracting (U*D*V)[0,j] entries for Fin 1/Fin 2 matrices via Matrix.mul_apply + Fin.sum_univ",
      "SNF 1x2 proof: A 0 j = u * d * V 0 j where u = U 0 0 (+-1) and d = D 0 0",
      "Part 1 (d|gcd): d|a and d|b since a = d*(u*V00), b = d*(u*V01), then Int.dvd_gcd",
      "Part 2 (gcd|d): det(V)=+-1 gives a*V11 - b*V10 = u*d*det(V) = +-d, then gcd|a and gcd|b gives gcd|d",
      "Key Lean tactics: congr_fun (congr_fun hsnf 0) j for entry extraction, Matrix.mul_apply + Fin.sum for expansion",
      "Proof uses entry extraction from A=UDV via congr_fun, det_fin_one/two, and Fin.sum_univ simplification",
      "2026-04-27 (researcher-4): SNF existence axiom is reducible over PIDs — Submodule.smithNormalForm in Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.FreeModule.PID provides this constructively. Restricting to ℤ recovers snf_exists as a specialization, eliminating one of two axioms in the parent file.",
      "2026-04-27: 1×2 proof structure generalizes cleanly: Int.gcd_dvd_left ↦ GCDMonoid.gcd_dvd_left; det V = ±1 ↦ IsUnit (det V) collapses 4-way case split to single IsUnit argument; Matrix.det_fin_two and congr_fun entry extraction are typeclass-free.",
      "2026-04-27: snf_solvability_criterion likely stays axiomatized over PIDs — full derivation needs quotient-module + Submodule.smithNormalForm theory (substantial separate development).",
      "2026-04-27: Recommended approach: wrapper file BezoutIdentityOQ04OQ01OQ01.lean parameterized by R [CommRing R] [IsPrincipalIdealRing R] [GCDMonoid R], recovering the ℤ case as R = ℤ specialization."
